      "problem": "Let $b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find $-\\frac{1}{2}b.$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying each component of $b$ by $-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}b & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
